<PolicyLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <p>This policy explains how the site operator handles personal information on VeloGroupsets. The operator and monitored contact address appear below once community submissions open. We apply the rights and obligations required by the privacy laws that apply to our operation; this policy does not assume that every visitor is covered by the same law.</p>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Information we collect</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6"><li>From Google sign-in: your verified email address and Google account identifier. We do not receive your Google password or request access to Gmail, Drive or your contacts.</li><li>Your chosen public display name, account status, necessary session records, and the version and time of your policy acceptances.</li><li>Your submitted photos, captions, image descriptions, component references, review decisions and upload timestamps.</li><li>Reports and correspondence, including a reporter’s contact details if they choose to provide them.</li><li>Our infrastructure providers process request information such as IP addresses, device/browser details and security signals. The application does not keep raw IP addresses in the community database.</li></ul></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What becomes public</h2><p class="mt-3">Approved photos, their captions and image descriptions, component references, public display names and upload dates are public. Your account email, Google identifier, sessions, reports and moderation correspondence are not published. Pending or rejected photos are not public.</p><p class="mt-3">We re-encode accepted photos and remove embedded metadata, including EXIF and GPS data, before storage. This does not remove information visible in the image itself: faces, registration plates, addresses, reflections and landmarks can still identify people or locations. Crop those out before uploading.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Why we use it</h2><p class="mt-3">We use this information to authenticate accounts, publish and attribute photos, prevent abuse, enforce upload limits, review reports, respond to rights requests and meet legal obligations. Where GDPR applies, these activities may rely on providing the service you request, proportionate legitimate interests in security and moderation, and legal obligations. We seek separate consent where the applicable law requires it; accepting the terms is not blanket consent to unrelated uses or marketing.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Providers and international processing</h2><p class="mt-3">Google provides sign-in. Cloudflare provides hosting, D1 account/metadata storage, R2 image storage, image transformations, Turnstile abuse prevention and the CSAM Scanning Tool. These providers may process information internationally. We do not promise that all information stays in Australia. We use appropriate safeguards required by applicable law and respond to requests for information about relevant transfers.</p><p class="mt-3">Cloudflare’s CSAM tool compares images entering its cache against known abusive-image lists. It supplements moderation and does not establish that every image is lawful or safe. Reports and legally required information may be shared with appropriate authorities. See <ExternalLink class="text-link" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</ExternalLink> and <ExternalLink class="text-link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s Privacy Policy</ExternalLink>.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Cookies and local storage</h2><p class="mt-3">Essential cookies keep sign-in requests and sessions secure. Sign-in requests expire after ten minutes and sessions after 30 days, or sooner on logout or suspension. The theme preference uses local storage. Turnstile uses security signals under Cloudflare’s policy. If Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled, its cookie-free beacon measures page usage; we do not use it to publish individual user activity or sell personal information.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Retention and removal</h2><p class="mt-3">Original uploaded files are processed in memory and are not retained in R2. Only the sanitised JPEG is stored. Unpublished submissions normally expire after seven days. Approved photos remain until removed. Removing a photo stops delivery through the site immediately; we delete the public object and request removal from the image CDN’s cache. Copies already downloaded or stored in other parties’ caches cannot always be recalled.</p><p class="mt-3">We retain account and consent records while needed to operate the account and handle disputes. Moderation and report records are restricted to authorised operators and retained only as needed to investigate, respond to requests or comply with law. Where lawful preservation is required, an authorised moderator can place a sanitised copy and relevant records in a private evidence hold. Holds are reviewed by the operator and are not used for public display or ordinary backups. Contact us for a case-specific retention or deletion response.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Your requests and complaints</h2><p class="mt-3">Contact us to request access, correction, account closure, removal or deletion of your information. Depending on the law that applies, you may also have rights to object, restrict processing, receive portable information or withdraw a consent. We may need proportionate identity verification and may retain information where the law permits or requires it. We will explain any refusal and the available complaint options.</p><p class="mt-3">You may complain to the <ExternalLink class="text-link" href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</ExternalLink> where it has jurisdiction, or to the relevant privacy authority in your country. If a breach triggers notification obligations, we will assess and make the required notifications.</p></section>
</PolicyLayout>
